# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Local working data: captures, downloads, render output, safety copies.
# Gigabyte-scale or regenerated; they belong to the working copy, not git.
#   data/       source captures (data/raw) and the prepared-scene cache
#   downloads/  source photos and licences of captures
#   out/        scratch figures (build.py --look, inspect_ply)
#   backup/     copies of tilesets taken before re-exporting
#   frames/     sweeps written by the viewer's capture button
# The data/ rule is anchored with a leading slash on purpose: an unanchored
# 'data/' also matches web/data/, and git cannot re-include files inside an
# excluded folder, so the tileset exceptions below would silently do nothing.
/data/
/downloads/
/out/
/backup/
/frames/
*.ply
*.zip

# A working copy's own capture presets (bozkir/presets.py) and its notes on
# captures that are not published.
capture_presets.local.json
docs/captures.md

# Presentation material outside the project: an unlinked draft page.
web/explain.html

# Exported tilesets and height fields. Two tilesets are public: the desert
# (its splats, manifest, height field, sediment and far-field atlas) and the
# river (splats, manifest, atlas; its terrain is generated in the browser),
# with the river's water tiles, so a fresh clone or the live page opens on
# real ground without a 10-minute export. The starter needs no file. Every
# other tileset, height field and the folder's index.json stay in the working
# copy that made them (python scripts/build.py data/raw/<name>.ply --preset
# <name>); the viewer looks for the desert whether or not an index is there.
web/data/*
!web/data/desert.*
!web/data/river.*
!web/data/water.json
!web/data/water.png
!web/data/water_deep.png

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
